{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New Jersey Security Deposit Law deposit cap, interest and return","requirement":"A landlord may not take a security deposit above one and one-half times one month's rent, may increase it by at most 10% a year, owes the tenant the interest earned, and must return the deposit with an itemized list of deductions within 30 days of move-out.","key_value":"1.5 months' rent; 10%/year increase; return within 30 days","coverage_conditions":"Residential rental tenancies in New Jersey. A landlord need not collect a deposit, but if one is taken these rules apply.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Seasonal use or rental of 125 consecutive days or fewer by a person with a permanent residence elsewhere is exempt from the deposit-account rules, but not housing for seasonal, temporary or migrant farm workers.","penalty":"Tenant may sue for double the amount wrongfully withheld plus court costs and reasonable attorney's fees; if the landlord fails to pay interest or give required notice, the tenant may apply the deposit plus 7% interest to rent and the landlord may not demand an additional deposit.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month’s rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Safe Housing Act security deposit return after domestic-violence termination","requirement":"When a tenant ends a lease under the Safe Housing Act, the landlord must make the security deposit and any interest available within 15 business days and, within 3 business days, notify the tenant in writing where and when to collect it.","key_value":"15 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants who terminate a lease under the Safe Housing Act because of domestic violence. Transient or seasonal rentals are not covered.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"Within 15 business days after the lease is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant’s security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant’s agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
